<h3>Confirm RTO (Regional Transport Office) Clearance</h3>
<p><strong>Key verification actions:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Match the vehicle’s registration number with the RTO database.</li>
<li>Verify there are no pending fines, suspensions, or black‑listing notices.</li>
<li>Check that the vehicle class and load capacity align with declared specifications.</li>
<li>Red‑flag: missing or altered registration documents suggest fraud.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Verify Insurance Proof</h3>
<p><strong>Key verification actions:</strong></div></div>
<ul>
<li>Obtain the policy document and confirm insurer name, policy number, and validity dates.</li>
<li>Ensure coverage includes third‑party liability, cargo, and comprehensive loss for the tracking period.</li>
<li>Check for any lapse in coverage; an expired policy violates regulations.</li>
<li>Red‑flag: generic PDFs without official letterhead or digital signatures.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Authenticate Driver Credentials</h3>
<p><strong>Key verification actions:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Validate the driver’s license number on the national transport authority portal.</li>
<li>Confirm the driver holds the correct endorsement for the vehicle type.</li>
<li>Review background‑check reports for criminal records or serious traffic violations.</li>
<li>Red‑flag: mismatched name/photo or a license nearing expiration.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Ensure GPS Activation and Data Integrity</h3>
<p><strong>Key verification actions:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Verify the GPS unit is factory‑installed, tamper‑sealed, and registered with the provider.</li>
<li>Test real‑time location updates; delays over 30 seconds may indicate spoofing.</li>
<li>Confirm data transmission uses encrypted channels (TLS/SSL).</li>
<li>Red‑flag: static coordinates, frequent signal loss, or unregistered IMEI numbers.</li>
</ul>

<p>Completing each step safeguards your fleet, ensures compliance with national vehicle transport regulations, and builds confidence in the tracking system.</p></div>
